IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eoa-dates`
IMPORT `eoa-rules`
IMPORT `eoa-seat`

-- Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic) -- cases for the questions in eoa-seat.l4. Every expected value was worked by hand
-- from the deposited text (the section is named on each group), not copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: see NOTES.md and SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.

§ `Cases`

§§ `ss 6, 7 -- the basis of the treatment`

#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `age` `an attribute I have now` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `pregnancy` `an attribute I had in the past` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `race` `a characteristic generally imputed to people with the attribute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `sexual orientation` `an attribute I am presumed to have or to have had` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `disability` `my assistance aid, helper or assistance dog` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `sex` `my assistance aid, helper or assistance dog` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `age` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was I treated on the basis of a protected attribute` `none of these attributes` `an attribute I have now` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 8, 9, 12 -- direct and indirect discrimination`

-- s 8 example 1: an employee refused training as "too old": unfavourable, age a substantial reason.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `age` `an attribute I have now` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Unfavourable, but the attribute not a substantial reason: s 8(2)(b) "provided that it is a substantial reason".
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `age` `an attribute I have now` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not treated unfavourably and no requirement.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `sex` `an attribute I have now` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 9 example 2: fluent English for a cleaning job; not proved reasonable.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `race` `an attribute I have now` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same requirement, proved reasonable (s 9(2)).
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `race` `an attribute I have now` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A requirement that does not disadvantage people with the attribute.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `race` `an attribute I have now` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Direct discrimination, but a proved special measure (s 12(2)).
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `race` `an attribute I have now` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Indirect discrimination does not depend on the basis: "something else" still gives it.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `disability` `something else` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Direct on "something else": s 7(2) does not say (NOTHING); no indirect case either.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `disability` `something else` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No attribute at all: neither.
#ASSERT `Was I discriminated against` `none of these attributes` `an attribute I have now` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Is it a special measure` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it a special measure` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is it a special measure` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 12(7): once the purpose is achieved it ceases to be one.
#ASSERT `Is it a special measure` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Part 4 Divisions 1 and 2 -- prohibited discrimination at work`

-- An employee dismissed because of pregnancy, no exception proved (s 18(b)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `an employee` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, with an exception proved (s 13).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `an employee` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not discrimination.
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `an employee` `some other detriment` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A job applicant refused the job (s 16(c)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a job applicant` `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A job applicant and "some other detriment": s 16 has no catch-all.
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a job applicant` `some other detriment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An employee and the terms offered: s 18 does not list it (s 16 does, for applicants).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `an employee` `the terms offered to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A contract worker not allowed to continue (s 21(1)(b)); s 21(2) not met.
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a contract worker` `not allowing me to work or continue to work` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, but it would be lawful if the worker's own employer did it (s 21(2)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a contract worker` `not allowing me to work or continue to work` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A partner expelled by a firm of 5 partners (s 31(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a partner in a firm` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A firm of 4 partners, reasonably (s 31(4)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a partner in a firm` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A firm of 4 partners, unreasonably: no prohibition (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a partner in a firm` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A firm being established: only the terms of the invitation (s 30(1)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a person invited to join a firm being established` `the terms offered to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a person invited to join a firm being established` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A union member whose membership terms were varied (s 35(2)(c)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a member of an industrial organisation` `varying the terms of my membership or qualification` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A qualifying body revoking a licence (s 36(1)(d)).
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a person dealing with a qualifying body` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A qualifying body and a training program: s 36 does not list it.
#ASSERT `Is it prohibited discrimination at work` `a person dealing with a qualifying body` `denying me a guidance, apprenticeship or training program` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 17, 19, 22, 32 -- accommodating parent or carer responsibilities`

#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `a person offered employment` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `a contract worker` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A reasonable refusal: outside "unreasonably" (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `an employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A job applicant not yet offered the job: s 17 speaks of "a person offered employment".
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `a job applicant` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A partner in a firm of 5 or more (s 32) and of 4 (none).
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `a partner in a firm` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `a partner in a firm` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No caring responsibilities.
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `an employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A union member: no such duty.
#ASSERT `Was the refusal to accommodate my caring responsibilities unlawful` `a member of an industrial organisation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 20, 22A, 33 -- reasonable adjustments`

#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `a contract worker` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 33 has no 5-partner threshold.
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `a partner in a firm` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless" the person could not do the work even after them.
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 20(5) disability standard; s 20(6) building determination.
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An unreasonable adjustment (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No adjustment needed; no disability.
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `an employee` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A job applicant not yet offered: s 20(1)(a) "is offered employment or is an employee".
#ASSERT `Must they make this adjustment for my disability` `a job applicant` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 23, 34 -- the disability exception`

-- An employee needing an unreasonable adjustment; the employer met s 20 otherwise.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `an employee` `disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The same, but the employer did not comply with s 20 (s 23(b)).
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `an employee` `disability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A job applicant (s 20 does not apply): (b) does not arise.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `a job applicant` `disability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Neither limb of (c).
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `an employee` `disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not disability.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `an employee` `age` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A partner in a 5-partner firm with caring responsibilities: s 34(b) asks for s 32 compliance (finding 3).
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `a partner in a firm` `disability` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `a partner in a firm` `disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A partner without caring responsibilities: s 32 does not apply, so (b) does not arise, whatever the s 33 position.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `a partner in a firm` `disability` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A union member: not an area of ss 16, 18, 30, 31.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the disability exception` `a member of an industrial organisation` `disability` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 24 to 29, 37 -- the other employment exceptions`

-- s 24 example: a client asks the agency for a female carer in her home.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the domestic services exception` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` TRUE `in a client's home, at the client's request` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the domestic services exception` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` TRUE `in the employer's own home` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the domestic services exception` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` TRUE `in a client's home, without the client's request` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the domestic services exception` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` TRUE `in a client's home, at the client's request` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not "determining who should be offered": the terms of the offer.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the domestic services exception` `a job applicant` `the terms offered to me` TRUE `in the employer's own home` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the domestic services exception` `an employee` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` TRUE `in the employer's own home` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can they rely on the care of children exception` `an employee` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the care of children exception` `a job applicant` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the care of children exception` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the care of children exception` `a contract worker` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 26(2)(c): searches of the bodies of people of that sex.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a job applicant` `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification` `sex` `searching the clothing or bodies of that sex` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a job applicant` `refusing or failing to give me the job, membership or qualification` `sex` `no genuine occupational requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(3): an actor's role limited by race for authenticity.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` `race` `no genuine occupational requirement` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` `race` `no genuine occupational requirement` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(4): physical features in modelling work.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a person offered employment` `the terms offered to me` `physical features` `no genuine occupational requirement` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a person offered employment` `the terms offered to me` `physical features` `no genuine occupational requirement` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 26(5): profession.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` `profession trade or occupation` `no genuine occupational requirement` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An attribute s 26 does not name.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `a job applicant` `deciding who should be offered the job, partnership or membership` `religious belief or activity` `no genuine occupational requirement` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An employee's dismissal: not the offering of employment.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on a genuine occupational requirement` `an employee` `dismissing or expelling me, or taking away my membership or qualification` `sex` `searching the clothing or bodies of that sex` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can they rely on the political employment exception` `a job applicant` `political belief or activity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the political employment exception` `a job applicant` `political belief or activity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the political employment exception` `a job applicant` `religious belief or activity` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the political employment exception` `an employee` `political belief or activity` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 28 example 2: female counsellors for women who experienced family violence.
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the welfare services exception` `a job applicant` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the welfare services exception` `a job applicant` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the welfare services exception` `a job applicant` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the welfare services exception` `an employee` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 28A: under 21 at 20; not at 21.
#ASSERT `May I be paid a youth wage` `an employee` 20 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I be paid a youth wage` `an employee` 17 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I be paid a youth wage` `an employee` 21 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `May I be paid a youth wage` `a contract worker` 18 EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `Can they rely on the early retirement exception` `an employee` TRUE `age` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the early retirement exception` `an employee` FALSE `age` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the early retirement exception` `an employee` TRUE `sex` EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 37 example: clinical hours dispensed with for a health professional with a disability.
#ASSERT `Can the qualifying body rely on the reasonable terms exception` `a person dealing with a qualifying body` `disability` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the qualifying body rely on the reasonable terms exception` `a person dealing with a qualifying body` `disability` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the qualifying body rely on the reasonable terms exception` `an employee` `disability` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Part 5 -- general exceptions`

#ASSERT `Can they rely on the statutory authority exception` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the statutory authority exception` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the statutory authority exception` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `Can they rely on the religious employment exception` TRUE `religious belief or activity` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the religious employment exception` TRUE `religious belief or activity` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can they rely on the religious employment exception` TRUE `religious belief or activity` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
